From b9726838913dbcde49a0369c3885f88a50279703 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 09:50:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] NMS: hide the treble_app foreground-service notification

RestlessOS runs the treble_app as a freezer-exempt foreground service so
device-specific sensor listeners (motorola chop-chop, handwave/pocket doze)
keep firing with the screen off. that service posts a persistent
foreground-service notification that some users want gone -- the same end
state as manually disabling notifications for the app.

android deliberately floors foreground-service notifications at IMPORTANCE_LOW
so users always see them, and an app cannot self-lock its channel importance to
bypass the floor (the system strips app-supplied lock fields on channel creation).
so suppress the treble_app notification at the system level instead: when an
fgs/uij notification is posted for me.phh.treble.app, force its record importance
to IMPORTANCE_NONE so it is not displayed.

the notification is still posted, so the fgs stays foreground -- startForeground()
clears the fgs anr timer via the call itself, and ams never demotes a fgs whose
notification is suppressed -- keeping the process unfrozen. all other fgs/uij
notifications (music, calls, downloads, ...) keep the standard LOW importance
floor and remain visible.
---
 .../notification/NotificationManagerService.java      | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/notification/NotificationManagerService.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/notification/NotificationManagerService.java
index a499054ac..210029ebb 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/notification/NotificationManagerService.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/notification/NotificationManagerService.java
@@ -8918,7 +8918,16 @@ public class NotificationManagerService extends SystemService {
         boolean isImportanceFixed = mPermissionHelper.isPermissionFixed(pkg, userId);
         r.setImportanceFixed(isImportanceFixed);
         if (notification.isFgsOrUij()) {
-            if (((channel.getUserLockedFields() & NotificationChannel.USER_LOCKED_IMPORTANCE) == 0
+            // restlessos: suppress the treble_app foreground-service notification.
+            // force the record importance to NONE so it is not displayed, while still
+            // posting it (the fgs stays foreground -- startForeground clears the anr
+            // timer and ams never demotes a fgs whose notification is suppressed, so
+            // the process stays unfrozen). all other fgs/uij notifications keep the
+            // standard LOW importance floor so music, calls, downloads etc. remain
+            // visible.
+            if ("me.phh.treble.app".equals(pkg)) {
+                r.setSystemImportance(IMPORTANCE_NONE);
+            } else if (((channel.getUserLockedFields() & NotificationChannel.USER_LOCKED_IMPORTANCE) == 0
                         || !channel.isUserVisibleTaskShown())
                     && (r.getImportance() == IMPORTANCE_MIN
                             || r.getImportance() == IMPORTANCE_NONE)) {
